### Run the API Server
```bash
cd server/annotations
pip install -r requirements.txt
python annotation_api.py
# Unit tests
python -m pytest tests/test_annotations.py -v

# Integration tests
python -m pytest tests/test_integration.py -v

# Live demo
python examples/usage_example.py
Annotations
POST /api/library-items/{id}/annotations - Create annotation
GET /api/library-items/{id}/annotations - Get annotations
PUT /api/annotations/{id} - Update annotation
DELETE /api/annotations/{id} - Delete annotation
Bookmarks
POST /api/library-items/{id}/bookmarks - Create bookmark
GET /api/library-items/{id}/bookmarks - Get bookmarks
DELETE /api/bookmarks/{id} - Delete bookmark
Data Management
GET /api/library-items/{id}/export - Export all data
POST /api/library-items/{id}/import - Import data
GET /api/health - Health check
Integration with LitLyric
This system is designed to complement LitLyric v0.6.1's new ebook reader features:

Compatible with Readium - Uses the same CFI format for EPUB positioning
PDF Support - Handles page-based positioning for PDF files
AudioBookShelf Ready - API structure designed for easy integration
Progress Tracking - Can be combined with existing updateEbookProgress functionality
Data Models
EbookLocation
# EPUB CFI location
EbookLocation(type=LocationType.CFI, value="/6/4[chap01]!/4/2/1:10")

# PDF page location  
EbookLocation(type=LocationType.PAGE, value=42)
Annotation
Annotation(
    id="ann-123",
    library_item_id="book-456", 
    user_id="user-789",
    start_location=start_location,
    text="Selected text content",
    note="User's note",
    color="#ffff00"
)
Bookmark
Bookmark(
    id="bm-123",
    library_item_id="book-456",
    user_id="user-789",
    location=location,
    title="Chapter 3 Start",
    note="Beginning of technical section"
)
